  "disposition": "COMPLETE_TYPED_FUNCTION_OR_EQUALITY_SEAMS_MATERIALIZED_UNCOMPILED",
  "review_notes": [
    "Each1527B original and3111B organized source read separately in full. MatrixAction has all eleven exact fields: Spin,stored DecidableEq,id,comp,inv,act plus five actual action/shape equations. No field is narrowed and decEqSpin is not newly registered as an instance.",
    "The composition equation is exactly act(comp g h)M=act h(act g M), including its order. inv_act_left is exactly act(inv g)(act g M)=M. Identity and both dimension preservation equations remain universal over the original BinaryMatrix. No group associativity, two-sided Spin inverse/unit law, faithful action, entry permutation, finite Spin or concrete rectangle geometry is supplied or inferred.",
    "One complete mathematical seam retains the whole dependent MatrixAction interface. The second retains the complete Unit copyAction with all five original proof bodies and exact copyAction_id_act projection, using only an explicit import of the same-source interface. External historical BinaryMatrix and Spin imports remain unchanged.",
    "RectV4ActionContract stores a MatrixAction, a type equivalence action.Spin equiv RectSpin and a runtime_semantics String; it does not relate action operations to tag composition or define any actual rectangular transformation. rectV4ActionContractTarget is an unproved existential with a True second component, not a constructed action. Both stay whole exact archives; no runtime metadata module is materialized."
  ],
